WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.044 --> 00:00:02.294
(laughing)

00:00:03.218 --> 00:00:05.825
- Laughter is like a
spiritual practice for me.

00:00:05.825 --> 00:00:07.825
I laugh everywhere I go.

00:00:09.477 --> 00:00:13.157
What I believe, the world
can be a better place

00:00:13.157 --> 00:00:15.505
if more and more people start laughing.

00:00:15.505 --> 00:00:17.755
(laughing)

00:00:20.944 --> 00:00:23.839
(chanting)

00:00:23.839 --> 00:00:25.386
My name is Madan Kataria.

00:00:25.386 --> 00:00:28.828
I'm a medical doctor and
creator of Laughter Yoga.

00:00:28.828 --> 00:00:31.104
(laughing)

00:00:31.104 --> 00:00:33.046
It's time to laugh.

00:00:33.046 --> 00:00:35.282
Laughter Yoga is a unique concept

00:00:35.282 --> 00:00:38.326
where anyone can laugh
for no reason at all.

00:00:38.326 --> 00:00:39.688
(laughing)

00:00:39.688 --> 00:00:43.626
We don't need to rely on jokes,
sense of humor or comedies.

00:00:43.626 --> 00:00:46.718
Laughter unwinds the
negative effects of stress

00:00:46.718 --> 00:00:49.337
and makes our immune system stronger.

00:00:49.337 --> 00:00:52.033
And brings more oxygen
to our body and brain.

00:00:52.033 --> 00:00:54.190
(laughing)

00:00:54.190 --> 00:00:55.996
The reason we call it Laughter Yoga

00:00:55.996 --> 00:00:59.272
is it's a combination
of laughter exercises

00:00:59.272 --> 00:01:01.596
with deep breathing techniques from yoga.

00:01:01.596 --> 00:01:04.283
Scientifically, our body
doesn't know the difference

00:01:04.283 --> 00:01:07.289
between real laughter and fake laughter.

00:01:07.289 --> 00:01:09.429
We will still get the
same health benefits.

00:01:09.429 --> 00:01:11.679
(laughing)

00:01:13.252 --> 00:01:17.417
I created Laughter Yoga because
my life was very stressful.

00:01:17.417 --> 00:01:19.268
Being a leader of a health magazine

00:01:19.268 --> 00:01:22.277
and a medical practitioner,

00:01:22.277 --> 00:01:25.791
I could not find any
relief from the stress.

00:01:25.791 --> 00:01:28.360
Then I found a breakthrough

00:01:28.360 --> 00:01:31.286
that there is lot of medicine in laughter.

00:01:31.286 --> 00:01:36.113
Based on this idea I created
laughter as a form of exercise.

00:01:36.113 --> 00:01:37.593
(laughing)

00:01:37.593 --> 00:01:40.027
I wake up at four in the
morning and the first thing I do

00:01:40.027 --> 00:01:43.475
is I laugh for 30, 40 minutes everyday.

00:01:43.475 --> 00:01:45.810
I'm laughing in my daily routine,

00:01:45.810 --> 00:01:47.229
laughing with my staff.

00:01:47.229 --> 00:01:48.542
(laughing)

00:01:48.542 --> 00:01:50.926
Everybody calls me, nobody says me hello.

00:01:50.926 --> 00:01:52.800
(laughing)

00:01:52.800 --> 00:01:53.651
Hoho-haha.

00:01:53.651 --> 00:01:55.574
(laughing)

00:01:55.574 --> 00:01:59.275
I'm laughing on Skype; I'm
teaching Laughter Yoga.

00:01:59.275 --> 00:02:00.542
One day I'm going to die laughing.

00:02:00.542 --> 00:02:02.752
(laughing)

00:02:02.752 --> 00:02:05.497
Very good, very good, yay.

00:02:05.497 --> 00:02:07.901
(laughing)

00:02:07.901 --> 00:02:10.570
My mission in life is to
create social laughter clubs,

00:02:10.570 --> 00:02:12.846
which are free for everyone in the world.

00:02:12.846 --> 00:02:15.061
(guitar music)

00:02:15.061 --> 00:02:18.120
When we laugh in a group it
becomes real and contagious,

00:02:18.120 --> 00:02:19.832
it becomes easier to laugh.

00:02:19.832 --> 00:02:23.936
Now we have more than
16,000 laughter clubs

00:02:23.936 --> 00:02:25.492
in 100 countries.

00:02:25.492 --> 00:02:27.186
(laughing)

00:02:27.186 --> 00:02:31.019
When you find happiness
with laughter practice,

00:02:32.780 --> 00:02:35.357
the perception of the algorithm changes.

00:02:35.357 --> 00:02:38.502
We can create happiness within ourselves.

00:02:38.502 --> 00:02:40.752
(laughing)

